The licence above covers this repository's own files: the program around the
emulator (waterbox/), the tests and the documents.

It does not cover VICE. VICE (extern/vice, a submodule: vice-libretro, the
libretro port of VICE, by the VICE team and the libretro authors) is under
the GNU General Public License, version 2 or later. The files under patches/
are changes to it and are under the same licence. waterbox/libm/ holds
musl's math functions, under the MIT licence (waterbox/libm/COPYRIGHT-musl).

The built package, vice.chimeraCore, holds VICE compiled together with this
repository's program, and is distributed under the GNU General Public License
version 2 or later. It holds the C64's and the 1541's ROMs that VICE itself
carries, as VICE distributes them, and no game.
